{number: 51}
{title: I Am Thine, O Lord}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I am Thine, O Lord, I have [F] heard Thy voice,
And it [C] told Thy love to [G7] me;
But I [C] long to rise in the [F] arms of faith,
And be [C] closer [G7] drawn to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Draw me [C] nearer, nearer, blessed [F] Lord,
To the [C] cross where Thou hast [G7] died;
Draw me [C] nearer, nearer, nearer, [F] blessed Lord,
To Thy [C] precious, [G7] bleeding [C] side.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Consecrate me now to Thy [F] service, Lord,
By the [C] pow'r of grace di-[G7] vine;
Let my [C] soul look up with a [F] steadfast hope,
And my [C] will be [G7] lost in [C] Thine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O the [C] pure delight of a [F] single hour
That be-[C] fore Thy throne I [G7] spend;
When I [C] kneel in prayer, and with [F] Thee, my God,
I com-[C] mune as [G7] friend with [C] friend!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
There are [C] depths of love that I [F] cannot know
Till I [C] cross the narrow [G7] sea;
There are [C] heights of joy that I [F] may not reach
Till I [C] rest in [G7] peace with [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
